====== U-Boot ======

To get the device bootable you need an additional u-boot Image suited for the boot device of your choice.\\
Choose beetwen "SolidRun" Builds or "OpenWRT" Builds.

  * SolidRun U-Boot Builds can be found at [[https://images.solid-run.com/A38X/U-Boot]]

^ u-boot image ^ boot device ^
| u-boot-clearfog-base-emmc-boot0.kwb \\ u-boot-clearfog-pro-emmc-boot0.kwb | eMMC boot from "boot0" Partition (4MiB, 2MiB used - Start: 0, End: 4095)\\ device: /dev/mmcblk0boot0 |
| u-boot-clearfog-base-emmc-boot1.kwb \\ u-boot-clearfog-pro-emmc-boot1.kwb | eMMC boot from "boot1" Partition (4MiB, 2MiB used - Start: 0, End: 4095)\\ device: /dev/mmcblk0boot1 |
| u-boot-clearfog-base-emmc.kwb \\ u-boot-clearfog-pro-emmc.kwb | eMMC boot from Data Partition (2MiB used - Start: 4096, End: 8191) !!! MBR on Sector 0. Keep Sector 4096 to 8192 free. First Partition needs to begin on Sector 8192. Do not use GPT. !!! \\ device: /dev/mmcblk0 |
| u-boot-clearfog-base-sata.kwb \\ u-boot-clearfog-pro-sata.kwb | SATA boot from Boot Sector (Size of "kwb" File used - Start: 1, End: <2048) \\ device: /dev/sda |
